# Development

How we develop day to day. Stack layout belongs in `init` / `file-policy`; this rule covers runtime workflow.

## Local stack (stub)

- Infra lives under `infra/` (Compose, Docker, Traefik).
- Apps: `apps/backend`, `apps/frontend`, `apps/prisma`.
- Prefer running services via the agreed Compose setup once it exists; do not invent ad-hoc containers without updating docs/rules.

## Environment variables (stub)

- Secrets never committed. Use `.env` locally; commit only `.env.example` without secrets.
- Document new env vars (name, required/optional, which app) and propose a rules update per `init`.
- TODO: canonical list of env vars per app and Compose.

## Docker / Compose (stub)

- Dockerfiles: `infra/docker`.
- Compose files: `infra/compose`.
- Traefik: `infra/traefik`.
- TODO: how to start the full stack, which ports, hot-reload vs container rebuild.

## Day-to-day habits

- Change only what the task needs; match existing style in neighboring files.
- Install dependencies inside the relevant `apps/<app>` unless a root workspace is defined.
- Do not commit or push unless explicitly asked.

